<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesPeriodPastDueAxis_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesEqualToGreaterThan90DaysPastDueMember_Kx27UqVIVESRgMYZ4QVzJA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableExcludingAccruedInterestBeforeAllowanceForCreditLossFeeAndLoanInProcess" scale="3" id="Tc_VQvbPk06XkO15WhtwgJgow_11_9">444</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.66%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.05%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;margin:0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:6.62%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_OZPY_o6nckS7uCXf_-4gjQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableExcludingAccruedInterestBeforeAllowanceForCreditLossFeeAndLoanInProcess" scale="3" id="Tc_Yzirl3z-lkSFWsP84QF2uQ_11_12">276,341</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.66%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:8pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.09%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;margin:0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:6.84%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:8pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_OZPY_o6nckS7uCXf_-4gjQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentNonaccrualStatus" scale="3" id="Tc_ju2az0JAxkGJohKT8avZEg_11_15">1,294</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;background:#ffff00;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">There were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_loan_NNFRge4OVUK7FRaUh30gVQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesPeriodPastDueAxis_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesEqualToGreaterThan90DaysPastDueMember_MVpubBy4jUWZEsbpOSRsKw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:NumberOfParticipationLoansPastDueAndStillAccruing" scale="0" id="Narr_n4uBNZ2Y8EyGVJIiUiLjHQ">29</ix:nonFraction> participation loans with a balance of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesPeriodPastDueAxis_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesEqualToGreaterThan90DaysPastDueMember_MVpubBy4jUWZEsbpOSRsKw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableExcludingAccruedInterest90DaysOrMorePastDueStillAccruing" scale="0" id="Narr_mHugEHTWqU-Zq5ZxWBkuRQ">24,962</ix:nonFraction> that had no related allowance that were 90+&#160;days past due and accruing interest at June 30, 2026 and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_loan_NNFRge4OVUK7FRaUh30gVQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesPeriodPastDueAxis_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablesEqualToGreaterThan90DaysPastDueMember_Kx27UqVIVESRgMYZ4QVzJA" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="hyne:NumberOfParticipationLoansPastDueAndStillAccruing" scale="0" id="Narr_y_ZpPODxl0ycAx3IX-5C1g">none</ix:nonFraction> as of December&#160;31, 2025. As of June 30, 2026, there was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_loan_NNFRge4OVUK7FRaUh30gVQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember_hrSwmbSI60egyEDUo3T5Wg" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="hyne:NumberOfNonAccrualLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_9PQXGNM4xUGq5rYCJQTSMw">one</ix:nonFraction> non-accrual loan in the one to four residential class with a balance of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember_hrSwmbSI60egyEDUo3T5Wg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:NonAccrualLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_zywOjGUUTUipk4t87N4mRg">254,790</ix:nonFraction> that had a related allowance of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember_hrSwmbSI60egyEDUo3T5Wg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:NonAccrualLoansRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_p0K6Dt5ejEibobjjO30Ozw">164,863</ix:nonFraction>. As of December 31, 2025, there was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_loan_NNFRge4OVUK7FRaUh30gVQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember__lw250pt6UuYvCNACL5uuA" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="hyne:NumberOfNonAccrualLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_YkwECpc6AECb6W8NqlzYdQ">one</ix:nonFraction> non-accrual loan in the one to four residential class with a balance of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember__lw250pt6UuYvCNACL5uuA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:NonAccrualLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_5NDYNam1ikuvRy5JY6ADkA">257,044</ix:nonFraction> that had a related allowance of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_FinancingReceivablePortfolioSegmentAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialPortfolioSegmentMember_us-gaap_FinancingReceivableRecordedInvestmentByClassOfFinancingReceivableAxis_us-gaap_ResidentialRealEstateMember__lw250pt6UuYvCNACL5uuA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:NonAccrualLoansRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_L3di0rxE4UaG1rX3_Eci0w">50,958</ix:nonFraction>. No material amount of accrued interest was written off by reversing interest income during the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 or 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">When, for economic or legal reasons related to the borrower&#8217;s financial difficulties, the Bank grants a concession to the borrower that the Bank would not otherwise consider, the modified loan is classified as a troubled loan modification (TLM). TLMs may consist of forgiveness of interest and/or principal, a reduction of the interest rate, interest-only payments for a period of time, and/or the extension of amortization terms. There were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_lY1umejnrU-KT0EsEUnUsw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsPostModificationRecordedInvestment2" scale="3" id="Narr_DLwAoHv9SUW8WRrkccD7Vw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_jIkQDJF0iEaKJHNOjZbF7g" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsPostModificationRecordedInvestment2" scale="3" id="Narr_gWU9QAh0UU2JWJSUtsAo6w"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_hu4aKIDnDEWp9X0JT67BDA" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsPostModificationRecordedInvestment2" scale="3" id="Narr_TZepIunDK0y1q_LvBl7DSA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_OSfTKmRx2U2OhX8RBRNwAw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsPostModificationRecordedInvestment2" scale="3" id="Narr_BZbWNSqz5k6X7-bO5XmjVw">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> new TLMs in the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 or 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Bank considers a TLM in default if it becomes past due more than 30&#160;days. <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_lY1umejnrU-KT0EsEUnUsw" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsSubsequentDefaultRecordedInvestment1" scale="0" id="Narr_j5z-bWEZ-kWkJSdDAgPWcw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_jIkQDJF0iEaKJHNOjZbF7g" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsSubsequentDefaultRecordedInvestment1" scale="0" id="Narr_o03y1hsgMESlid_XQsrdEg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_hu4aKIDnDEWp9X0JT67BDA" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsSubsequentDefaultRecordedInvestment1" scale="0" id="Narr_KQhl1Cwr5USRgCDfWK-_HQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_OSfTKmRx2U2OhX8RBRNwAw" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableModificationsSubsequentDefaultRecordedInvestment1" scale="0" id="Narr_EvIeurEs702mpiNKrYozFA">No</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> TLMs defaulted within 12&#160;months of their modification date during the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 or 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">There were no significant changes in the extent to which collateral secured our collateral dependent loans as of June 30, 2026 and December&#160;31, 2025. At June 30, 2026 and December&#160;31, 2025, we had approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_-yvQzg-CV0yh_wrIFa0_7g" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:FinancingReceivableCollateralDependentLoansNoRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_2xrxe38qB0-AOcBd6Yjh5w">280,749</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_OZPY_o6nckS7uCXf_-4gjQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="hyne:FinancingReceivableCollateralDependentLoansNoRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_G-MJZyrPHEaYjWf0_okuuQ">27,650</ix:nonFraction>, respectively, of residential real-estate collateral dependent loans without an allowance and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_-yvQzg-CV0yh_wrIFa0_7g" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="hyne:FinancingReceivableCollateralDependentLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_K3Pf-q0-x0SWYf4eAo8gDQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_OZPY_o6nckS7uCXf_-4gjQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="hyne:FinancingReceivableCollateralDependentLoansWithRelatedAllowance" scale="0" id="Narr_hd3usuQ_gUWQHAFpeJWZ0g">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> collateral dependent loans with an allowance.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Bank has <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_-yvQzg-CV0yh_wrIFa0_7g" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:LoansAndLeasesReceivableImpairedCommitmentToLend" scale="0" id="Narr_mc_jtUkaU06A77fR_WYB9Q">no</ix:nonFraction> commitments to loan additional funds to borrowers whose loans have been determined to be collateral dependent.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">There were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_-yvQzg-CV0yh_wrIFa0_7g" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:MortgageLoansInProcessOfForeclosureAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_rmwlOlZqNEeyVWwx7JtuRg">no</ix:nonFraction> mortgage loans in the process of foreclosure at June 30, 2026, and an aggregate of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_DYxuJxWTOEmd_sKITldJgQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_OZPY_o6nckS7uCXf_-4gjQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:MortgageLoansInProcessOfForeclosureAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_9DptFBMfSk6L11n7YTfrLQ">324,000</ix:nonFraction> in principal amount of mortgage loans in the process of foreclosure at December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">15</p></div></div>
